# Ownership. Later rules win, so the shared paths at the bottom override the
# per-owner rules above them.
#
# This file is the single source of truth for the split. `blast-radius stubs`
# parses it to group work by owner, and core/tests/test_stub_inventory.py fails
# if a source directory is not covered here.
#
# See CLAUDE.md and AGENTS.md for the same table in prose, and CONTRIBUTING.md
# for the branch convention.

# Default: everything not listed below needs both of us.
*                                   @etka @teammate

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# OWNER A — etka — the engine
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/core/                              @etka
/skill/                             @etka

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# OWNER B — teammate — CI, environment, the Action
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/ci/                                @teammate
/env/                               @teammate
/.github/workflows/                 @teammate

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# SHARED — changing any of this changes the interface between the two halves.
# Both owners must approve. Frozen after day 1; see CONTRACT.md.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/contracts/                         @etka @teammate
/README.md                          @etka @teammate
/CONTRACT.md                        @etka @teammate
/CONTRIBUTING.md                    @etka @teammate
/AGENTS.md                          @etka @teammate
/CLAUDE.md                          @etka @teammate
/pyproject.toml                     @etka @teammate
/Makefile                           @etka @teammate
/.github/CODEOWNERS                 @etka @teammate

# examples/ is append-only; each side writes into its own subfolder.
/examples/README.md                 @etka @teammate
/examples/reports/                  @etka
/examples/fixes/                    @etka
